# Implementation Plan - Nucleus HUD Production Config Fix

## Problem
The `nucleus-hud` frontend is failing to connect to the backend in production because it defaults to `http://localhost:5055`. This happens because `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL` is not passed as a build argument in the Dockerfile or Cloud Build configuration.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This requires a redeploy of the `nucleus-hud` service. I will also trigger a build of the backend to ensure consistency, but the primary change is to the frontend build process.

## Proposed Changes

### Build Configuration

#### [MODIFY] [cloudbuild.yaml](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/cloudbuild.yaml)
- Add `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL` to the `nucleus-hud` build arguments.
- Ensure `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` is also correctly passed.

#### [MODIFY] [Dockerfile](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/Dockerfile)
- Add `ARG NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL`
- Add `ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL=$NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL`

## Verification Plan

### Automated Build & Deploy
Run the following command to deploy the fixes:
```bash
gcloud builds submit --config cloudbuild.yaml \
  --substitutions=_NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://nucleus-orchestrator-7an2ps6yna-uc.a.run.app,_NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_API_URL=https://nucleus.gentlequest.app \
  .
```

### Manual Verification
1.  Visit `https://nucleus-hud-7an2ps6yna-uc.a.run.app`
2.  Open Chrome DevTools -> Network Tab.
3.  Verify calls to `https://nucleus.gentlequest.app` (instead of localhost).
4.  Verify calls to `https://nucleus-orchestrator-7an2ps6yna-uc.a.run.app`.
